.TH LCD-COMMANDS 1 "2026-07-16" "gway-001" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lcd-commands \- local LCD lockfile display tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lcd-lockfile-runner
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B lcd-system-info-publisher
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B gway-eth0-node-lcd-monitor
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The local LCD stack is independent of the Arthexis Python runtime. Producers
write small lockfiles, and
.B lcd-lockfile-runner
rotates those lockfiles onto the attached 16x2 LCD.
.PP
.B lcd-system-info-publisher
generates the normal ten-screen system-information rotation.
.PP
.B gway-eth0-node-lcd-monitor
can publish information about a node attached on eth0.
.SH LOCKFILES
The runner reads lockfiles from
.IR /home/arthe/.local/state/lcd-lockfiles
and, for compatibility, the legacy Arthexis lock directory when configured.
.PP
Important files include:
.TP
.I lcd-channels.lck
Channel order, such as
.BR "script summary" .
.TP
.I lcd-rotation.script
Scripted rotation frames used by the system-info publisher.
.TP
.I lcd-event-*.lck
High-priority event messages that temporarily preempt normal rotation.
.SH LCD-LOCKFILE-RUNNER OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --lock-dir " DIR"
Add a lock directory. May be repeated.
.TP
.BI --rotation-seconds " SECONDS"
Normal frame duration. The local default is 10 seconds.
.TP
.BI --event-seconds " SECONDS"
Event frame duration.
.TP
.BI --poll-seconds " SECONDS"
Refresh and scroll interval.
.TP
.B --no-hardware
Write fallback state/history only.
.TP
.B --stop-embedded
Stop old embedded Arthexis LCD runner processes owned by this user.
.TP
.B --once
Render one selected frame and exit.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Print the selected frame instead of writing the LCD.
.SH SYSTEM-INFO PUBLISHER OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --lock-dir " DIR"
Output directory for generated LCD lockfiles.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Print the ten generated frames without writing lockfiles.
.SH EXAMPLES
Show the generated ten-screen rotation:
.PP
.nf
/home/arthe/.local/bin/lcd-system-info-publisher --dry-run
.fi
.PP
Publish system-info frames immediately:
.PP
.nf
/home/arthe/.local/bin/lcd-system-info-publisher
.fi
.PP
Render one LCD frame without hardware writes:
.PP
.nf
/home/arthe/.local/bin/lcd-lockfile-runner --once --dry-run --no-hardware
.fi
.PP
Check the active LCD services:
.PP
.nf
systemctl --user status lcd-lockfile.service --no-pager
systemctl --user status lcd-system-info-publisher.timer --no-pager
.fi
.PP
Inspect the fallback current-screen file:
.PP
.nf
cat /home/arthe/.local/state/lcd-lockfile-runner/lcd-screen.txt
.fi
.SH CURRENT ROTATION
The current system-info rotation includes host, network, Wi-Fi, health, disk,
power, services/process count, devices, logs, and work state. When the summary
channel is active, the runner alternates system-info frames with summary frames.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /home/arthe/.local/bin/lcd-lockfile-runner
Standalone LCD runner.
.TP
.I /home/arthe/.local/bin/lcd-system-info-publisher
System-info frame publisher.
.TP
.I /home/arthe/.local/state/lcd-lockfiles
Local LCD lockfile directory.
.TP
.I /home/arthe/.local/state/lcd-lockfile-runner
Runner state, history, and fallback display files.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR sound-commands (1)
